    const caption=`Each cell shows one protein’s ${quantity} at one Qwen size. Read across a row to follow the same protein as Qwen gets larger. The two model heatmaps have the same rows and score scale. The difference is ${shortModelLabel(state.a)} minus ${shortModelLabel(state.b)}: positive cells mean a larger displayed value with ${shortModelLabel(state.a)}, negative cells with ${shortModelLabel(state.b)}. Its colorbar is centered at zero. B denotes billions of nominal parameters.`;
